&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;November 14, 2025-Redmond, OR&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&mdash; Redmond Fire &amp;amp; Rescue is proud to announce its partnership with the Kiwanis Club of Redmond for this year&rsquo;s Food Drive. This community initiative aims to provide essential food items to local families in need during the holiday season.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The food drive will run from November through&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;December 31, with the collection point at &lt;strong&gt;Redmond Fire &amp;amp; Rescue's downtown station, located at 341 NW Dogwood Ave.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Donations of non-perishable food items such as canned goods, pasta, rice, and boxed meals are encouraged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;Our mission goes beyond emergency response&mdash;we&rsquo;re committed to supporting the community in every way we can,&rdquo; said Ryan Herrera, Fire Chief of Redmond Fire &amp;amp; Rescue. &ldquo;Partnering with the Kiwanis Club of Redmond allows us to make a real difference for families during the holidays.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Kiwanis Club of Redmond has a long-standing tradition of serving the community, and this collaboration strengthens efforts to ensure no family goes hungry this Thanksgiving.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How to Help&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Drop off non-perishable food items at Redmond Fire &amp;amp; Rescues downtown station.&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Share this initiative on social media to spread the word.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-left: 40px;"&gt;Salem, Oregon &ndash; Grant awards totaling $ 1,759,580 will be distributed to 355 Oregon arts organizations through the Oregon Arts Commission&rsquo;s Sustaining Arts Program for fiscal year 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-left: 40px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-left: 40px;"&gt;In 2025, the Arts Commission reimagined this grant program to provide a more equitable distribution of funds to arts organizations. Awards are determined based on a newly updated funding formula that considers an organization&rsquo;s annual expenses, number of applications and available grant funds. Grant awards range from $1,000 to $20,000, and these unrestricted awards are available to nonprofit arts organizations that offer public arts programs throughout the year.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-left: 40px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

