&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;
The Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU) is a specialized unit responsible for investigating fatal and critical injury collisions on Oregon&rsquo;s highways. The team provides expertise in the documentation, investigation, and analysis of complex motor vehicle crashes and crime scenes. They receive specialized training in the use of advanced measuring techniques and small unmanned aircraft systems (sUAS) for on-scene investigations. The CRU team includes ACTAR accredited collision reconstructionists and technical collision investigators deployed across the state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Concert November 12 at 7:00 p.m. &mdash; Tickets $15&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Oregon-based pop artist &lt;strong&gt;Hannah Wood&lt;/strong&gt; brings her powerful voice and vibrant stage presence to the &lt;strong&gt;Chemeketa Auditorium&lt;/strong&gt; on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#FF0000"&gt;Wednesday&lt;/span&gt;, November 12 at 7:00 p.m.&lt;/strong&gt; as part of the college&rsquo;s Wonder Wednesdays concert series.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Known for her &lt;strong&gt;witty lyricism, charismatic performance style, and genre-bending pop sound&lt;/strong&gt;, Hannah Wood is one of Oregon&rsquo;s most exciting new artists. Her debut album, &lt;em&gt;Hello to a Woman&lt;/em&gt;, has been nominated for &lt;strong&gt;Best Pop, Synth, or Contemporary Album&lt;/strong&gt; at the &lt;strong&gt;2025 PNW Music Awards&lt;/strong&gt;, earning her recognition across the Pacific Northwest music scene.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Drawing inspiration from artists like &lt;strong&gt;Lizzy McAlpine&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Kacey Musgraves&lt;/strong&gt;, Wood crafts emotionally rich, radio-ready songs that blend authenticity with a contemporary pop edge. Her clear and expressive vocals, paired with her signature storytelling, make her live shows both intimate and electric.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;We&rsquo;re thrilled to bring Hannah to the Chemeketa stage,&rdquo; said Stephen Munshaw, Auditorium Manager at Chemeketa Community College. &ldquo;She represents the incredible local talent thriving in Oregon&rsquo;s music scene, and audiences are in for a memorable night of fresh, heartfelt pop music.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

